# One-shot import markers are LOCAL state. The email-pattern import adds to
# existing counts rather than replacing them, so a fresh clone that inherited
# a "already imported" marker would skip a real import — and one that
# inherited nothing would double-count. Keep it per-machine.
data/imports/.*_imported

# ---- Private: never commit, this repo is PUBLIC -------------------------
# Real people's names, private assessments of them, personal research, and
# the founder's own target list. Scrubbed from history 2026-08-02; these
# rules stop them coming back. Local copies live here and are backed up to
# ~/Desktop/coverage-private-not-in-git.
docs/research/
data/
scripts/import_hk_coffee_chats.py
scripts/seed_founder.py

# Undo journals from data-changing management commands. `backfill_contact_regions`
# defaults its `--undo-file` to `region_backfill_undo_<timestamp>.json` in the
# CURRENT DIRECTORY, which for a `manage.py` run is `coverage_web/` — beside the
# source, where an untracked file is easy to sweep into a `git add`. One already
# was (866d95b), and it carried the founder's email address and 34 of his live
# contact IDs mapped to regions into this public repo.
#
# Ignored rather than relocated: the journal is what `--revert` reads, so it has
# to survive on the machine that wrote it. It just must never travel.
*_undo_*.json

# Legal drafts. Never tracked: this is a public repo.
docs/liam-safe-draft-*.md

# enrich_contact_regions / backfill_contact_regions: per-run plan and undo files (contain real names + URLs)
region_enrich_plan_*.json
region_enrich_undo_*.json
region_backfill_undo_*.json
